      "message": "We won\u0027t, we\u0027ll end up creating the same type again, and when we return up the new type will be the same as the old type.\n\nIt\u0027s tricky to validate that each struct has a changed member, we\u0027d need to store a second hash because we map from original struct currently. But we\u0027re walking modified structs here, which means we\u0027d need a way to to from modified struct back to original.\n\nGiven that it seems easier to just always return a type, it will be de-dup\u0027d by the type manager, and then we change if it\u0027s new.",
